From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 02:57:11 +0200
Subject: media: gc2145: Fix AWB measure window register page

The AWB big window registers are 0xec to 0xef on page 0, but they were
written on page 1. So the window kept its power-on default and four
undocumented page 1 registers got written instead.

The datasheet lists them as P0:0xec..0xef ("Big win use by AWB") and
the vendor init sequence writes them directly after selecting page 0.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
@@ -1715,11 +1715,11 @@ static int gc2145_setup_awb(struct gc2145_dev *sensor,
 	// load awb settings
 	gc2145_set_registers(sensor, (void*)gc2145_awb_regs, sizeof(gc2145_awb_regs));
 
-	// awb window
-	gc2145_write(sensor, 0x1ec, x1 / ratio);
-	gc2145_write(sensor, 0x1ed, y1 / ratio);
-	gc2145_write(sensor, 0x1ee, x2 / ratio);
-	gc2145_write(sensor, 0x1ef, y2 / ratio);
+	// awb window (big window, page 0)
+	gc2145_write(sensor, 0x0ec, x1 / ratio);
+	gc2145_write(sensor, 0x0ed, y1 / ratio);
+	gc2145_write(sensor, 0x0ee, x2 / ratio);
+	gc2145_write(sensor, 0x0ef, y2 / ratio);
 
 	// eanble awb
 	gc2145_update_bits(sensor, 0x82, BIT(1), BIT(1));
